      "content": "The most effective approach is to integrate both national achievements and critical examinations of systemic injustices. A curriculum that only celebrates triumphs creates a sanitized, unrealistic view of the past, which is intellectually dishonest. By teaching about both the successes and the struggles, students develop a nuanced understanding of how societies function and evolve, fostering informed, engaged citizenship.",
