      "content": "Focusing solely on power struggles risks creating a constant narrative of victimhood, which undermines the necessary sense of shared civic identity. A strong curriculum must teach that progress is built upon both aspiration and struggle, not just conflict. By highlighting shared values alongside historical challenges, students learn to be active participants in improving their nation, rather than just perpetual critics of it.",
      "source": "target",
