    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but you keep saying it has to be \"both.\" if we're being honest, isn't it true that emphasizing systemic injustice is more \"effective\" at preparing kids for the real world and making them better citizens, whereas the \"shared values\" approach is really just outdated propaganda meant to avoid the hard truths?",
